  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe test `a_tapered_punch_is_refused_at_post_while_the_file_states_no_guide_heights` in `crates/app/tests/sodick_alc400g.rs` had a stale expectation. The product is not changed.\n\nCause: PR #1818 (commit `ceafc0f8f`, the fix for #1800) added `wire_edm::taper_door` to `wire_gate`. Now `CreateOperation` refuses a tapered Wire Contour when the machine states no guide heights. Before, the first refusal came at the post. The test expected the create step to pass and failed at its `expect` (line 145). The taper is still refused, and it is refused earlier. No program was posted.\n\nThe test now pins two refusals:\n\n1. The command door: `CreateOperation` with a 5 degree taper on the shipped ALC400G file is refused with `states no edm.lower_guide_z and edm.upper_guide_z` and `set the taper to 0`.\n2. The post (defence in depth): the op is made on a copy of the file with guide heights (TEST ONLY figures). Then the shipped file is mounted again. `post_script` must refuse with the guide-height words.\n\nThe rule of #1856 stays true: a tapered punch with no guide heights in the machine file is refused at post.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Before the change (on `62e1d36a6`, Windows, debug): the test fails with `5 deg is inside the 25 deg limit: \"Invalid(\\\"a 5.000 degree taper is asked, and machine Sodick ALC400G states no edm.lower_guide_z and edm.upper_guide_z - ...; set the taper to 0\\\")\"`. The failure is not flaky and not specific to the Linux runner.\n- After the change: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test sodick_alc400g`: 5 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test sodick_alc400g -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `sodick_alc400g::a_tapered_punch_is_refused_at_post_while_the_file_states_no_guide_heights`\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The batch tier and the post-merge run. The issue closes only when a post-merge run on `main` is green.\n- Release mode and Linux. The test has no platform-specific code.\n\nChangelog: none (test only)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1856\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
